Instructions to Remove SD Card Functionality from main.c

1. Find and remove the SD card header include (likely near the top of the file):
   Search for and remove this line:
   ```c
   #include "sdcard_handler.h"
   ```

2. Find and remove the SD card initialization call (likely in main() function):
   Search for and remove these lines:
   ```c
   /* Initialize SD card */
   sdcard_init();
   ```
   or any similar call to sdcard_init() function.

3. If you find any other SD card related functions or code (like test code),
   you should remove those as well.

These changes, together with the ones already made to:
- prj.conf (removing SD card config options)
- build.sh (removing SDMMC overlay reference)
- CMakeLists.txt (removing sdcard_handler.c from sources)

should completely eliminate the SD card functionality from the build and
prevent the MPU fault that was occurring in the system workqueue thread.